capture: don't make the capture overlay a utility window on X11, so KWin makes it fullscreen.

Flameshot runs under XWayland here, seen as an X11 session (see configure_flameshot in
scripts/lib/provision/services.sh). There its overlay is a Qt::Tool window, a utility window to
the window manager. KWin only makes normal windows and dialogs fullscreen, so it turns down the
overlay's request and fits it into the area the panel leaves free: the taskbar stays out of the
overlay, and can't be selected or drawn on. As a normal window it goes fullscreen, over the panel.

Applied by scripts/patches/patch-flameshot, see provision.

diff --git a/src/widgets/capture/capturewidget.cpp b/src/widgets/capture/capturewidget.cpp
index 3d18398..a4eba1e 100644
--- a/src/widgets/capture/capturewidget.cpp
+++ b/src/widgets/capture/capturewidget.cpp
@@ -184,8 +184,9 @@ CaptureWidget::CaptureWidget(const CaptureRequest& req,
         } else {
             // Note: Qt::BypassWindowManagerHint is removed to fix x11 gnome
             // crash. It's needed on Cosmic
-            setWindowFlags(Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint | Qt::FramelessWindowHint |
-                           Qt::Tool);
+            // No Qt::Tool: KWin won't make a utility window fullscreen, which
+            // leaves the panel uncovered.
+            setWindowFlags(Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint | Qt::FramelessWindowHint);
         }
 #endif
 
